It is Saturday afternoon.
I am in my flat.
Suddenly, I hear a strange sound from the bedroom.
I go inside and look.
Asha's dog Moti is sitting on the rug.
He is happily chewing my sandal.
I immediately clap my hands.
"Moti, no!" I say loudly.
"Drop it right now!"
Moti looks at me with big eyes.
"Give it to me," I say to him.
"Chewing shoes is forbidden!"
Moti slowly drops the sandal from his mouth.
I quickly pick up my sandal.
Then I bring his favourite toy.
"Take this, Moti," I say to him.
"You must chew this."
Moti happily takes the toy.
I look at my sandal.
Fortunately, it is absolutely fine.
